(>> Solution to Question 17:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine common tense errors in the Results and Discussion sections of graduate biotechnology theses.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Problem of Tense Oscillation:) Tj
T*
(   A widespread flaw in student manuscripts is erratic tense oscillation within the same) Tj
T*
(   paragraph???jumping ungrammatically between Past Simple, Present Simple, and Present Perfect:) Tj
T*
(   - Flawed Passage: "We centrifuged the lysate at 14,000 rpm. The supernatant is collected and) Tj
T*
(   has been analyzed by spectrophotometry. Table 2 showed that protein yield was 45 mg/L.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Linguistic Diagnosis & Correction:) Tj
T*
(   - Centrifuging and collecting are sequential past methodological actions -> Must be Past) Tj
T*
(   Simple.) Tj
T*
(   - Analyzing is a past methodological step -> Must be Past Simple.) Tj
T*
(   - Table 2 currently exists on the page -> Must be Present Simple.) Tj
T*
(   - The numerical finding is historical empirical data -> Past Simple.) Tj
T*
(   - Corrected Academic Passage: "We centrifuged the lysate at 14,000 rpm, collected the clear) Tj
T*
(   supernatant, and analyzed protein concentration via spectrophotometry. Table 2 shows that the) Tj
T*
(   final protein yield was 45 mg/L.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
