(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine errors in conditional sentence logic: the illicit insertion of 'would' in 'if'-clauses.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Illicit 'Would' Fallacy:) Tj
T*
(   A ubiquitous syntactic error among non-native and careless writers is inserting the modal) Tj
T*
(   'would' or 'would have' into the subordinate 'if'-clause:) Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical: "*If the researcher would calibrate the instrument, the results would be) Tj
T*
(   accurate.") Tj
T*
(   - Grammatical \(Second Conditional\): "If the researcher calibrated the instrument, the results) Tj
T*
(   would be accurate.") Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical: "*If the researcher would have calibrated the instrument, the results would) Tj
T*
(   have been accurate.") Tj
T*
(   - Grammatical \(Third Conditional\): "If the researcher had calibrated the instrument, the) Tj
T*
(   results would have been accurate.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Grammatical Rationale:) Tj
T*
(   The subordinate conditional clause \('protasis'\) establishes the hypothetical condition, which) Tj
T*
(   is morphologically marked by past or past-perfect inflections; the main clause \('apodosis'\)) Tj
T*
(   carries the modal verb expressing conditional consequence. Doubling 'would' destroys the) Tj
T*
(   syntactic dependency hierarchy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze how choice of tense controls authorial voice, distance, and epistemic stance in scientific peer reviews.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Concept of Epistemic Stance in Academic Writing:) Tj
T*
(   Epistemic stance refers to the degree of certainty, commitment, or cognitive distance an author) Tj
T*
(   expresses toward an empirical claim. Verb tense and aspect are paramount rhetorical vehicles) Tj
T*
(   for modulating this stance:) Tj
T*
